The web app bundles these libraries in src/gecaa/web/vendor, each with its
licence file:
  Leaflet 1.9.4 (BSD-2-Clause), Leaflet-Geoman free 2.17.0 (MIT),
  Cytoscape.js 3.30.2 (MIT).
Background map tiles come from basemap.de (c) BKG, licensed CC BY 4.0.

Version 2 queries these open services at run time (no data is bundled):
  Geobasis NRW: ALKIS vereinfacht WFS, DOP and ALKIS WMS (dl-de/zero-2-0);
  Geologischer Dienst NRW: Bodenkarte BK50 WMS (dl-de/by-2-0);
  LANUK NRW: Wasserschutzgebiete WMS (free; commercial use requires permission);
  BKG: Starkregengefahrenhinweise WMS (dl-de/by-2-0);
  OpenStreetMap Nominatim for address search (data (c) OpenStreetMap
  contributors, ODbL; used within the Nominatim usage policy).

Version 3 (climate risk) additionally uses at run time:
  Geobasis NRW: DGM1 terrain model WCS (dl-de/zero-2-0), ALKIS land use (WFS);
  Deutscher Wetterdienst: KOSTRA-DWD-2020 design rainfall and annual hot-day grids
  (opendata.dwd.de, CC BY 4.0);
  LANUK NRW: Klimaanalyse NRW WMS (dl-de/zero-2-0);
  BKG: Hinweiskarte Starkregengefahren, water depth (dl-de/by-2-0).

Portions of src/gecaa/risk (damage.py, scenario.py, cra.py) and data/climaax are
adapted from the CLIMAAX project (https://github.com/CLIMAAX: FLOODS, HEAVY_RAINFALL,
crabook), licensed Apache-2.0 OR CC-BY-4.0, (c) the CLIMAAX consortium. The JRC
depth-damage values originate from Huizinga, de Moel & Szewczyk (2017), EUR 28552 EN.

CLIMADA (https://github.com/CLIMADA-project/climada_python, (c) ETH Zurich and
contributors, GPL-3.0) is NOT part of GECAA. It runs as a separate service in
services/climada_worker, which is itself licensed GPL-3.0-or-later (see
services/climada_worker/LICENSE). GECAA exchanges only JSON data with it and also
runs without it (built-in fallback engine).

Version 4 adds:
  LISFLOOD-FP 8.1 (University of Bristol, GPL-2.0-only) - NOT part of GECAA; downloaded and built by
  services/lisflood_worker/install.sh and run as a separate program behind a GPL service. GECAA's own
  2D solver (src/gecaa/risk/inertial.py) implements the published local-inertial method of
  Bates, Horritt & Fewtrell (2010) independently.
  WhiteboxTools (MIT), xclim (Apache-2.0), xarray (Apache-2.0), pystac-client (Apache-2.0),
  planetary-computer (MIT), PySWMM (BSD-2-Clause) / EPA SWMM (public domain), pygeoapi (MIT),
  typst (Apache-2.0), MapLibre GL JS 4.7.1 (BSD-3-Clause, bundled in src/gecaa/web/vendor/maplibre).
  QGIS plugin in qgis_plugin/ is licensed GPL-2.0-or-later (QGIS API requirement).
  Data at run time: Geobasis NRW 3D building models LoD2 (dl-de/zero-2-0), INSPIRE Planned Land Use
  NRW / development plans (dl-de/by-2-0), Zensus 2022 100 m grid (Destatis, dl-de/by-2-0),
  DWD daily station data (CC BY 4.0), Landsat Collection 2 Level-2 via Microsoft Planetary Computer
